Subject: Mark UISourceCode as synthesized in StyleFile.addHeader

Previously, StylesSourceMapping only called
NetworkProject.setSourceURLSynthesized when a StyleFile was initially
constructed. If a stylesheet without a sourceURL comment was added first
and a synthetic stylesheet with a /*# sourceURL=... */ comment for the
same URL was added later via StyleFile.addHeader, the UISourceCode
remained unflagged even after the original stylesheet was removed.

Update StyleFile.addHeader to also mark the UISourceCode as having a
synthesized sourceURL when header.hasSourceURL is true, and add a
regression unit test.

Bug: 562233597, 568225269
Change-Id: Ie8bb7d38207987431c9823676cd6ec38bf514aa2
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8518358
Reviewed-by: Philip Pfaffe <pfaffe@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Eric Leese <leese@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
front_end/models/bindings/StylesSourceMapping.test.ts does not exist on this branch; its test-only hunk was dropped. The StylesSourceMapping.ts change applied unchanged.

diff --git a/front_end/models/bindings/StylesSourceMapping.ts b/front_end/models/bindings/StylesSourceMapping.ts
index d14a225f7687f93065048ceb8642e3b4aff51953..1b7119743757bb96fc9e36bd4de1498522fca647 100644
--- a/front_end/models/bindings/StylesSourceMapping.ts
+++ b/front_end/models/bindings/StylesSourceMapping.ts
@@ -191,6 +191,9 @@ export class StyleFile implements TextUtils.ContentProvider.ContentProvider {
 
   addHeader(header: SDK.CSSStyleSheetHeader.CSSStyleSheetHeader): void {
     this.headers.add(header);
